(The same drop on the other count in a format spec: `{f:.N}` read its
 precision with the same 32-bit parse, so a precision past i32::MAX printed
 the float at its default precision instead - a different number of decimal
 places than the one asked for, silently. LANGUAGE.md:3106 puts no ceiling
 on N either, so only a precision too large to hold is refused.)

a float called f is 3.5.
Print "{f:.18446744073709551616}".
